<title>USA: Moneygram Payment Systems Q1 net income off.</title>
<headline>Moneygram Payment Systems Q1 net income off.</headline>
<dateline>SADDLE BROOK, N.J. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>MONEYGRAM PAYMENT SYSTEMS INC</p>
<p>   Three months ended March 31	     1997		1996</p>
<p>Revenue</p>
<p>  Fee and other				 $26.3	     $27.6</p>
<p>  Foreign Exchange				6.1		 8.0</p>
<p> Total Revenue				   32.4		35.6</p>
<p>Expenses</p>
<p>  Agent Commissions			    11.0		11.0</p>
<p>  Processing					6.0		 6.4</p>
<p>  Advertising &amp; Promotion		     6.0		 8.8</p>
<p>  Selling &amp; Service			     3.0		 2.2</p>
<p>  General &amp; Administrative		    2.8		 1.8</p>
<p> Total Expenses				  28.8		30.2</p>
<p> Income Before Income Taxes		   3.6		 5.4</p>
<p> Income Tax Expense			     1.4		 2.0</p>
<p> Net Income					 2.2		 3.4</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share			     .13		 .20</p>
<p> Wgtd avg shrs outstanding		 16,625	    16,625</p>
<p>		  (in millions, except per-share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Net EPS matched First Call Q1 1997 estimate $0.13</p>
<p>Revenue fell to $32.4 million from $35.6 million in the year-earlier period due to a reduction in foreign exchange revenue on U.S.-to-Mexico money transfer transactions, the company said. Foreign exchange revenue fell by 24 percent to $6.1 million from $8.0 million in Q1 1996.</p>
</text>
